📊 Performance Goals

The project aims to evaluate:

- Order-matching latency.
- Median and 99th-percentile latency (P50 and P99).
- Orders processed per second.
- Memory allocation and data-copying overhead.
- Performance differences between Python and optimized Cython implementations.

Actual performance results will be published after benchmarking.

🔬 Research Focus

The project explores how zero-copy techniques, efficient data structures, and compiled extensions can reduce latency in high-frequency trading systems. It also investigates the trade-offs between development simplicity and predictable execution performance.

⚠️ Disclaimer

ChronosMatch is an educational and research project. It is intended for simulated trading and performance benchmarking, not live financial trading. No real-money trading or production-level performance is guaranteed.

